cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, methodology, or published search records, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "SETIsearch: Panchromatic (8.709-Octave, 0.0905-37.86 um) Space-Lyman to Spitzer/SOFIA EXES Mid-IR, JWST NIRISS/SOSS + NIRSpec/G140H, Coherent Shift-Stack Drift, Frequency-Comb, Radio & Photometric Technosignature Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Prospectively locked, reproducible archival searches and pure-stdlib numerical audits
  for panchromatic space Lyman-limit/FUV/NUV (FUSE 0.0905-0.1187 um, HST/COS G130M
  0.1125-0.1450 um, HST/STIS E140M 0.1145-0.1710 um, HST/STIS E230M/E230H 0.1605-0.3150 um),
  ground near-UV (VLT UVES_NUV), optical (HARPS, HARPS-N, ESPRESSO HR/UHR, Gemini GHOST
  BLUE+RED 0.348-1.061 um with simultaneous sky-IFU veto, Gemini GRACES, Euler CORALIE,
  OHP SOPHIE, OHP ELODIE, CFHT ESPaDOnS, MPG/ESO FEROS, VLT FLAMES/GIRAFFE HR), far-red
  (VLT UVES_RED, CARMENES_VIS with per-exposure CARACAL SERVAL RV alignment), 3-arm
  simultaneous UVB+VIS+NIR (VLT X-shooter 0.2989-2.4790 um), near-infrared YJH (NIRPS_HE),
  thermal J/H/K (VLT CRIRES+), SDSS APOGEE-2 H-band (up to N=28 visits), simultaneous YJHK
  (CFHT SPIRou APERO 0.7.295), JWST space optical-to-thermal-IR (NIRISS SOSS 0.68-2.83 um,
  NIRSpec G140H 0.95-1.88 um, NIRSpec G235H/G395H, MIRI LRS, MIRI MRS Ch1-4), airborne
  high-resolution mid-IR echelon-echelle (SOFIA EXES 5.62-26.13 um, R~86,000), and Spitzer
  IRS SL+LL (5.20-37.86356 um) laser, NaN-preserving coherent shift-stack curved/periodic
  multi-epoch drift (DRIFT_V54 across 20 N>=4 campaigns), greenhouse CCF, Dyson waste-heat
  vs. silicate-belt discrimination, and periodic frequency-comb technosignatures
  (0.0905-37.86356 um, 8.709 unbroken octaves across 27 spectrographs / 36 arms; 425 unique
  stars and 2,523 archival exposures totaling 751.6534 h across V3.0-V5.4 + COMB_V4_1 with
  Keplerian planetary de-Doppler across 138 orbital campaigns, 37,911 synthetic calibration
  trials, 313,257 Legacy V2 false alarms eliminated, deterministic Stage-2 physical triage,
  and uniform all-sky COMB_V4_1 filtering across 448 stacks), unified with 1.4 GHz
  Parkes/GBT radio searches and TESS photometry achieving 23/23 (100%) radio-echelle
  closure across a 425-system synthesis (0 verified ETI detections; 0.0973 W HST_STIS
  Proxima Cen, 0.039712 kW JWST_NIRISS_SOSS SIMP 0136, 0.114498 kW CARMENES_VIS LP 731-58,
  0.14238 kW JWST_NIRSPEC_G395H CWISEPJ1935, 0.20533 kW JWST_MIRI_LRS Luhman 16AB,
  34.509826 kW JWST_NIRSPEC_G140H VHS 1256 b, 202.381291 kW SOFIA_EXES Sirius 7.21 um, and
  52 calibrated panchromatic bridges across 719 cells [+ BD+60 1753 = 53 multi-phase targets]
  alongside 165 <10 pc stars with 1.5222 kW median limit).
